|item[steward-evident-register] :date 2026-07-28 :status parked :class vocabulary
  Coined and steward-approved this session ("perfect"): **steward-evident
  (formalization pending)** -- the epistemic state where the argument
  logic has become self-evident to the steward but is unaudited; distinct
  from derived-tier and from mere proposal. Two independent collisions
  with the existing tier ladder motivated it: Joseph's colloquial "first
  principles" usage, and TST's own "convergent representational choice"
  third category (which already has an open frontmatter-register
  proposal). Natural formal home: the three-axis epistemology's
  support-kind/register vocabulary, next time it gets worked. Until
  then: transcriptions render his "first principles" as steward-evident
  with the nearest formal carrier cited.
  |answer :by joseph :date 2026-07-28
    "sounds good for consideration later. Maybe I'll get disciplined enough that it won't be necessary ;-)"

